    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 5,
    "title": "Ask someone to do something",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk2-pivotal-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Ask someone to do something",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put the person after 请, 叫 or 让, followed by their action. That person receives the request and performs the second action. Naming someone is a separate use of 叫.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "老师让我看书。",
                "pinyin": "lǎoshī ràng wǒ kàn shū 。",
                "meaning": "The teacher asks me to read.",
                "audio": "494b5ff4276e9f4191f324c7ac2a9854e4c8ab0f0fc4a7cc2e2699079e9eb061"
              },
              {
                "text": "我请老师看。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ qǐng lǎoshī kàn 。",
                "meaning": "I ask the teacher to look.",
                "audio": "95c999fcc015e5f7a5b02e9018ecd9dedb04707d419c59609275ce19c6c93610"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
